## Day 7 — Command Injection + CSRF

### Command Injection
- User input executed as OS command
- Separators: ; && || | backtick
- Payload: 127.0.0.1; cat /etc/passwd
- Web shell: <?php system($_GET["cmd"]); ?>
- Fix: input validation + escapeshellarg()

### CSRF
- Forces authenticated user to make unwanted request
- One-way attack — attacker can't read response
- Example: hidden img tag triggers bank transfer
- Fix: CSRF tokens on every state-changing request

### Difference: XSS vs CSRF
- XSS: attacker injects code that runs in victim's browser
- CSRF: attacker tricks victim's browser into making requests

